{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784648155,"nonce":"8ryNS16mk4cxxAGW0NHFpmnEdFo=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe queued-thanks \"wait until the commit is public\" gate treats any HTTP\nresponse below 300 as \"published\", but cgit serves a **200 OK** for a\nmissing commit (the \"Bad object\" text lives in the response *body*), so the\ngate passes and the thanks is sent anyway.\n\n**The check** — `process_queue()` in `src/b4/ty.py:1079-1093`:\n\n    resp = session.head(checkurl, timeout=15, allow_redirects=True)\n    if resp.status_code \u003e= 300:\n        still_pending += 1\n        ...\n        continue\n    # falls through to send\n\nTwo compounding problems:\n\n1. **Wrong success signal.** cgit's `/commit/?id=\u003chash\u003e` returns `200 OK`\n   with an error page when the object isn't present; it does not 404. So\n   `status_code \u003e= 300` is never true for the reporter's unpublished commit,\n   and the code falls through to `send_mail()` (`ty.py:~1100`).\n2. **`HEAD`, not `GET`.** The request is `session.head()`, so even if the\n   body carried a machine-readable signal (\"Bad object\"), the code never\n   fetches or inspects it. The status line is the only thing consulted.\n\nThe `checkurl` itself is correct — it's built from `thanks-commit-url-mask`\nagainst the last taken commit (`_tracking_app.py:~4836`) and stored on the\nqueued message as the `X-Check-URL` header (`ty.py:964-966`). The UI's\n\"Queued — will send when commits are published\" promise\n(`_tracking_app.py:~4898`) is therefore real in intent but not enforced in\npractice.\n\n## Why \"checked by itself\" seemed to work\n\nThe reporter noted a non-queued send appeared to do the right thing. The\nnon-queued path (`_send_thank_message`, `_tracking_app.py:~4901`) performs\n**no** publish check at all — it just sends. So its \"correctness\" is\nincidental (the operator eyeballs it), not a second, working implementation\nof the check. The gate exists only on the queued path, and only there is it\nbroken.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nStandalone within the thanks/queue path. No fix suggestions per request.","files":null}]}